{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Scaling: Distributed Training, FSDP, DeepSpeed Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: Simulate Data Parallelism"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Split a batch across simulated GPUs. Each GPU computes a forward pass on its shard. Average the \"gradients\" (we simulate them as the loss values)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def simulate_data_parallelism(data, num_gpus, model_fn):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    batch_size = len(data)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    shard_size = batch_size // num_gpus"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    remainder = batch_size % num_gpus"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    gpu_losses = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    gpu_gradients = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    offset = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for gpu_id in range(num_gpus):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        extra = 1 if gpu_id < remainder else 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        shard = data[offset:offset + shard_size + extra]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        offset += shard_size + extra"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        loss, grad = model_fn(shard)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        gpu_losses.append(loss)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        gpu_gradients.append(grad)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    avg_loss = np.mean(gpu_losses)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    avg_gradient = np.mean(gpu_gradients, axis=0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return avg_loss, avg_gradient"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The all-reduce operation (averaging gradients) is the only communication in data parallelism. In practice, this uses the NCCL library on NVIDIA GPUs, which implements ring all-reduce: each GPU sends 1/N of its gradients to its neighbor, receives 1/N from the other neighbor, and after N-1 steps every GPU has the complete average. Total communication volume: 2 x gradient_size x (N-1)/N, approaching 2x the gradient size for large N."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: Simulate Tensor Parallelism"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Split a weight matrix across GPUs. Each GPU computes a partial matrix multiplication. Combine the results."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def simulate_tensor_parallelism(input_data, weight_matrix, num_gpus):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    d_in, d_out = weight_matrix.shape"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    assert d_out % num_gpus == 0, f\"d_out {d_out} not divisible by num_gpus {num_gpus}\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    shard_size = d_out // num_gpus"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    partial_results = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for gpu_id in range(num_gpus):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        start = gpu_id * shard_size"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        end = start + shard_size"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        weight_shard = weight_matrix[:, start:end]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        partial = input_data @ weight_shard"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        partial_results.append(partial)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    full_output = np.concatenate(partial_results, axis=-1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    direct_output = input_data @ weight_matrix"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    error = np.abs(full_output - direct_output).max()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return full_output, error"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The error should be exactly zero (or machine epsilon). Tensor parallelism is mathematically exact -- it produces the same result as computing the full matmul on one GPU. The split is along the output dimension, so each GPU produces a different chunk of columns, and concatenation reconstructs the full result."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "For column-parallel linear layers (splitting the output dimension), you concatenate. For row-parallel (splitting the input dimension), you sum. In a transformer FFN, the first linear (expand) uses column-parallel and the second linear (contract) uses row-parallel. This avoids an all-reduce between the two layers."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: Simulate Pipeline Parallelism"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Split a model's layers across virtual GPUs. Show the bubble problem where early stages sit idle while later stages compute."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def simulate_pipeline_parallelism(num_layers, num_stages, num_microbatches):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    layers_per_stage = num_layers // num_stages"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    timeline = {}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    clock = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for mb in range(num_microbatches):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for stage in range(num_stages):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            start_time = max("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                timeline.get((stage, mb - 1, \"fwd\"), (0, 0))[1] if mb > 0 else 0,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                timeline.get((stage - 1, mb, \"fwd\"), (0, 0))[1] if stage > 0 else 0,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            end_time = start_time + layers_per_stage"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            timeline[(stage, mb, \"fwd\")] = (start_time, end_time)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    last_fwd_end = max(v[1] for v in timeline.values())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for mb in range(num_microbatches - 1, -1, -1):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for stage in range(num_stages - 1, -1, -1):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            deps = [last_fwd_end]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if mb < num_microbatches - 1 and (stage, mb + 1, \"bwd\") in timeline:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                deps.append(timeline[(stage, mb + 1, \"bwd\")][1])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if stage < num_stages - 1 and (stage + 1, mb, \"bwd\") in timeline:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                deps.append(timeline[(stage + 1, mb, \"bwd\")][1])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            start_time = max(deps)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            end_time = start_time + layers_per_stage"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            timeline[(stage, mb, \"bwd\")] = (start_time, end_time)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    total_time = max(v[1] for v in timeline.values())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    compute_time = num_microbatches * num_stages * layers_per_stage * 2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    bubble_fraction = 1.0 - compute_time / (total_time * num_stages)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return timeline, total_time, bubble_fraction"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "With 4 stages and 1 micro-batch, the bubble fraction is 75% -- three out of four GPUs idle at any time. With 16 micro-batches, it drops to about 19%. The cost of eliminating bubbles is memory: you must store activations for all in-flight micro-batches simultaneously."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: Memory Calculator"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Compute the exact memory requirements for training any model size."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def memory_calculator("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    params_billions,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    precision_bytes=2,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    optimizer=\"adam\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    num_gpus=1,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    sharding=\"none\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    sequence_length=2048,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    batch_size_per_gpu=1,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    hidden_dim=None,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    num_layers=None,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    params = params_billions * 1e9"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    weight_memory = params * precision_bytes"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if optimizer == \"adam\":"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        optimizer_memory = params * 4 * 2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    elif optimizer == \"sgd\":"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        optimizer_memory = params * 4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    else:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        optimizer_memory = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    gradient_memory = params * precision_bytes"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    total_no_activation = weight_memory + optimizer_memory + gradient_memory"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if hidden_dim and num_layers:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        activation_per_layer = ("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            sequence_length * batch_size_per_gpu * hidden_dim * precision_bytes * 4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        activation_memory = activation_per_layer * num_layers"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    else:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        activation_memory = params * precision_bytes * 0.5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if sharding == \"fsdp\" or sharding == \"zero3\":"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        weight_memory /= num_gpus"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        optimizer_memory /= num_gpus"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        gradient_memory /= num_gpus"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    elif sharding == \"zero2\":"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        optimizer_memory /= num_gpus"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        gradient_memory /= num_gpus"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    elif sharding == \"zero1\":"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        optimizer_memory /= num_gpus"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    per_gpu_total = weight_memory + optimizer_memory + gradient_memory + activation_memory"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return {"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"params_billions\": params_billions,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"weights_gb\": weight_memory / 1e9,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"optimizer_gb\": optimizer_memory / 1e9,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"gradients_gb\": gradient_memory / 1e9,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"activations_gb\": activation_memory / 1e9,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"per_gpu_total_gb\": per_gpu_total / 1e9,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"total_across_gpus_gb\": per_gpu_total * num_gpus / 1e9,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"fits_on_80gb\": per_gpu_total / 1e9 <= 80,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"num_gpus\": num_gpus,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"sharding\": sharding,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    }"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "This calculator answers the question every ML engineer asks: \"How many GPUs do I need?\" Feed it the model size and see whether it fits. Adjust sharding strategy until the per-GPU total drops below 80GB."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: Mixed Precision Simulation"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Compare memory usage between FP32, FP16, and mixed precision training."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def mixed_precision_comparison(params_billions):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    params = params_billions * 1e9"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    fp32_weights = params * 4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    fp32_optimizer = params * 4 * 2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    fp32_gradients = params * 4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    fp32_total = fp32_weights + fp32_optimizer + fp32_gradients"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    fp16_weights = params * 2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    fp16_master = params * 4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    fp16_optimizer = params * 4 * 2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    fp16_gradients = params * 2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    fp16_total = fp16_weights + fp16_master + fp16_optimizer + fp16_gradients"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    mixed_weights = params * 2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    mixed_optimizer = params * 4 * 2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    mixed_gradients = params * 2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    mixed_total = mixed_weights + mixed_optimizer + mixed_gradients"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return {"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"fp32_total_gb\": fp32_total / 1e9,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"fp16_with_master_gb\": fp16_total / 1e9,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"mixed_bf16_gb\": mixed_total / 1e9,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"savings_vs_fp32\": 1 - mixed_total / fp32_total,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    }"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The biggest surprise for most people: mixed precision does not halve the memory. The optimizer states (Adam's m and v) stay in FP32 regardless of precision. For a 7B model, FP32 training uses 112GB. Mixed precision uses 84GB. That is a 25% reduction, not 50%. The optimizer dominates."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
